# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env (CLAUDE.md §8.5, §10).
#
# Local development: `npm run db:up` starts a local Postgres and prints a URL.
#
# Two separate credentials, deliberately (CLAUDE.md §8.1 — see db-init/01-app-role.sql
# for why): DATABASE_URL is the schema-owning role used only by `prisma migrate`/
# `generate`/seed. APP_DATABASE_URL is the restricted, non-superuser role the running
# application actually queries through — the one Row Level Security is real for. Never
# point APP_DATABASE_URL at the same role as DATABASE_URL.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/mou7asib?schema=public"
APP_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://app_user:password@localhost:5432/mou7asib?schema=public"

# Password-reset email (apps/web/lib/email.ts). Create a key at resend.com, no other
# config needed to start — it sends from Resend's own onboarding domain until a real
# sending domain is added and verified, which only delivers to the account owner's own
# verified email in the meantime.
RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."
# Optional — defaults to Resend's onboarding domain. Set this once a real domain is
# verified in the Resend dashboard.
# RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS="mou7asib <noreply@yourdomain.com>"

# Malware scanning (apps/web/lib/malwareScanner.ts, CLAUDE.md §8.4). clamd is always a
# separate daemon — never leave both unset in a deployed environment, since the local
# socket default (below) cannot resolve anywhere clamd isn't already running as a system
# service. Local dev: install clamav-daemon (see apps/ai/README.md's prerequisites) and
# leave these unset — it connects to the default local socket automatically.
# CLAMD_HOST="clamd.internal.example.com"
# CLAMD_PORT="3310"
# Only used on the local-socket path (no CLAMD_HOST set) — override if clamd's socket
# isn't at the Debian/Ubuntu default.
# CLAMD_SOCKET="/var/run/clamav/clamd.ctl"
